[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
**Weather and opening correlation**
<<<

[SYSTEM_REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SR-EXT-010
STATEMENT: >>>
When a configured frost, wind, rain, or storm policy is
active and a relevant opening is qualified, C-EXT shall raise or update
`ExternalWeatherExposure{HazardId}{OpeningId}` through
`sm_ext_weather_exposure` within `T_ext_decision`. A new exposure at an
external door, garage door, or gate shall require a known-open state for
`T_ext_door_open`, timed independently for each opening. A closed or unknown
contact shall reset this interval. An open window shall qualify immediately.
A valid, locally applicable official warning normalized as `immediate`
shall also qualify an open aperture configured for its hazard after the
shared hazard persistence interval.
C-EXT shall re-evaluate the contact and applicable evidence when the
interval elapses. An existing exposure shall follow the clear policy in
[LINK: SYS-SR-EXT-013, SYS-SR-EXT-013] and [LINK: SYS-SR-EXT-043, SYS-SR-EXT-043].
C-EXT shall qualify modeled hazards and applicable official warnings independently per provider and hazard
after continuous fresh threshold evidence for the configured persistence
interval (75 seconds for weather, independently 300 seconds for outdoor AQ by
default). Weather response shall complete within 120 seconds total from usable
input and a relevant known-open aperture: 5 s dispatch, concurrent weather and
opening qualification (75 s and 60 s), 9 s scheduling/reconciliation, 1 s decision
and 30 s notification allocation. Configured overrides shall fit this total;
provider polling and physical onset remain explicit boundaries.
An interruption shall reset pending
qualification. Official warnings, including `immediate` warnings, shall remain
authoritatively valid and fresh throughout that interval.
<<<
RELATIONS:
